"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#credentials-and-generated-files","content":"Fastlane writes `lamassu.yaml` in the current directory and injects credentials into it."},"185":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-107","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#credentials-and-generated-files","content":"Protect the generated values file, record the generated credentials in an appropriate secret store and do not reuse the evaluation identity setup in production."},"186":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-108","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#verify-the-installation","content":"Then open `https://pki.example.com` and sign in with the initial user. If the Gateway is programmed but the URL is unreachable, follow the checks in Expose the Gateway."},"187":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"page","content":"Install with Helm","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Deployment","Kubernetes self-managed"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm"},"188":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-0","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","content":"Prepare dependencies, configure the Lamassu chart and verify a controlled Kubernetes deployment."},"189":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-1","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#install-lamassu-with-helm","content":"Install Lamassu with Helm"},"190":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-2","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"Before you begin"},"191":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-3","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"1\\. Install the Gateway prerequisites"},"192":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-4","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"2\\. Create a values file"},"193":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-5","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#tls-with-an-existing-secret","content":"TLS with an existing Secret"},"194":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-6","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"Provision the first administrator"},"195":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-7","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#3-install-lamassu","content":"3\\. Install Lamassu"},"196":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-8","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#4-verify-the-deployment","content":"4\\. Verify the deployment"},"197":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-9","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"Production decisions"},"198":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-10","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#install-lamassu-with-helm","content":"Use the Helm workflow when you need explicit control over identity, databases, messaging, certificates, storage and upgrades. For an evaluation environment where the script can make those choices for you, use Fastlane."},"199":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-11","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"Prepare the platform services that are deliberately outside the Lamassu chart:"},"200":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-12","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"a Kubernetes 1.24+ cluster and Helm 3.2+"},"201":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-13","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"a reachable PostgreSQL server and a role allowed to create databases and schemas"},"202":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-14","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"a reachable RabbitMQ broker and credentials"},"203":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-15","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"an OIDC provider, normally Keycloak, with a realm/tenant and client for Lamassu"},"204":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-16","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"Envoy Gateway 1.8+ and a `GatewayClass`"},"205":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-17","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"cert-manager 1.14+; for trusted TLS, either a trusted issuer or a Kubernetes TLS Secret"},"206":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-18","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"a StorageClass and an external traffic design"},"207":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-19","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"The chart defaults to a `GatewayClass` named `eg`. Change `gateway.className` if your platform team uses another name."},"208":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-20","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"You provide the PostgreSQL server. The chart's pre-install job connects with the supplied credentials, creates the required `pki`, `authz` and `wfx` databases and service schemas, runs migrations, and applies `services.authz.bootstrap`."},"209":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-21","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"The chart has no Helm dependencies that install PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ, an OIDC provider, Envoy Gateway or cert-manager."},"210":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-22","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Install or upgrade the Envoy Gateway CRDs before its controller. The commands below match the version used by the Lamassu Helm repository:"},"211":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-23","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Create the default `GatewayClass` if it does not already exist. Save this manifest as `gateway-class.yaml`:"},"212":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-24","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Install cert-manager separately before Lamassu. The current chart renders its self-signed issuer and CA certificate resources even when `tls.type: external` makes the Gateway use an existing TLS Secret. Selecting external TLS therefore does not remove the cert-manager prerequisite."},"213":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-25","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"Start with the chart defaults and override the environment-specific values. This example assumes PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ and Keycloak are reachable through Kubernetes DNS, and exposes Keycloak at `/auth` through the shared Lamassu Gateway:"},"214":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-26","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"Do not add `gateway.addresses` by default. Leave address assignment to the load-balancer implementation unless your network design requires a specific Kubernetes-side VIP. The public IP of an upstream NAT gateway or reverse proxy does not belong in this value."},"215":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-27","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"If Keycloak is external and already has its own reachable URL, point the OIDC settings at it and omit the `/auth` entry from `gateway.extraRouting`."},"216":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-28","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#tls-with-an-existing-secret","content":"Create a Secret containing `tls.crt` and `tls.key`, then reference it:"},"217":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-29","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"There is no implicit superuser. Create the role or group expected by `services.authz.bootstrap` in the OIDC provider and assign it to at least one administrator before exposing Lamassu."},"218":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-30","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"The pre-install and pre-upgrade job applies the bootstrap idempotently: existing principals are preserved and missing grants are added."},"219":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-31","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"Test both an authorized identity and a denied identity. If no token matches an active bootstrap principal, nobody can administer the PKI."},"220":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-32","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"See Access control for the principal and policy model."},"221":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-33","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#3-install-lamassu","content":"To install a local checkout instead:"},"222":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-34","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#4-verify-the-deployment","content":"The Gateway should report `PROGRAMMED=True`. If it is programmed but has no usable address, continue with Expose the Gateway."},"223":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-35","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#4-verify-the-deployment","content":"The Helm test checks the CA, DMS Manager, Device Manager and VA health endpoints and verifies the UI response."},"224":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-36","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"Before going live, review:"},"225":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-37","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"backup and recovery for PostgreSQL and persistent volumes"},"226":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-38","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"a production KMS engine; the default filesystem engine is not an HA design"},"227":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-39","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"shared VA storage before increasing VA replicas"},"228":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-40","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"managed OIDC roles and removal of evaluation credentials"},"229":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-41","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"a trusted TLS issuer or externally managed certificate"},"230":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-42","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"resource requests, replicas, autoscaling, disruption budgets and placement"},"231":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-43","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"SMTP, observability and alert delivery"},"232":{"id":"/docs/d