36","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview#what-the-lamassu-chart-provides","content":"TLS"},"343":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview-37","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview#what-the-lamassu-chart-provides","content":"cert-manager `Issuer` and CA `Certificate` resources; either a chart-managed downstream `Certificate` or a reference to your TLS Secret"},"344":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview-38","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview#what-the-lamassu-chart-provides","content":"cert-manager itself; for trusted TLS, a trusted issuer or a populated TLS Secret"},"345":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview-39","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview#what-the-lamassu-chart-provides","content":"Persistent application data"},"346":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview-40","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview#what-the-lamassu-chart-provides","content":"PersistentVolumeClaims required by the default local KMS and VA storage"},"347":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview-41","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview#what-the-lamassu-chart-provides","content":"A StorageClass, physical storage, backups and a shared/external backend when scaling requires one"},"348":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview-42","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview#what-the-lamassu-chart-provides","content":"Optional integrations"},"349":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/overview-43","page_id":"/doc