encies and any provider resources already created if an operation fails partway through."},"2013":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-75","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#operations-on-a-key","content":"Each registered key has a detail view and several operational actions."},"2014":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-76","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#view-details","content":"The **View Details** screen concentrates the technical and administrative information of the key."},"2015":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-77","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#view-details","content":"The **Overview** tab shows, among others, these fields:"},"2016":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-78","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#view-details","content":"**Key Name**: descriptive name."},"2017":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-79","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#view-details","content":"**Key Identifier**: unique system identifier. Lamassu uses PKCS11-based ID formats."},"2018":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-80","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#view-details","content":"**Tags**: associated labels."},"2019":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-81","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#view-details","content":"**Aliases**: alternative names."},"2020":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-82","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#view-details","content":"**Crypto Engine**: engine where the key resides."},"2021":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-83","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#view-details","content":"**Algorithm, Key Size & Strength**: algorithm, parameters and strength level."},"2022":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-84","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#view-details","content":"The **Related Entities** section shows which Lamassu objects depend on that key."},"2023":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-85","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#view-details","content":"The **Public Key** tab shows public material in PEM. The record’s identifier and URI locate the key; a PKCS#11-formatted URI does not establish that the engine is an HSM or that a local module can access it."},"2024":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-86","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#sign-and-verify","content":"The **Sign / Verify** action validates that the key and the cryptographic engine work correctly."},"2025":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-87","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#sign-and-verify","content":"Sign a test message, save the signature and verify it using the same public key, algorithm and encoding. Then change the message: verification should fail. This tests one operation; it does not establish every engine capability or a CA’s chain."},"2026":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-88","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#sign-and-verify","content":"When you open it, two areas appear: **Sign** and **Verify**."},"2027":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-89","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#sign","content":"This tab uses the private key to generate a digital signature over a message or an already computed *digest*."},"2028":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-90","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#sign","content":"Main fields:"},"2029":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-91","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#sign","content":"**Algorithm**: signing algorithm available for the key type."},"2030":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-92","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#sign","content":"**Message Type**: `Raw` for clear data or `Digest` for a precomputed hash."},"2031":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-93","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#sign","content":"**Payload Encoding**: input encoding, such as UTF-8, Hex or Base64."},"2032":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-94","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#sign","content":"**Message**: content to sign."},"2033":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-95","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#sign","content":"**Signature**: result of the operation, shown in hexadecimal."},"2034":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-96","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#verify","content":"This tab checks whether a signature corresponds to the associated public key."},"2035":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-97","page