","PKI","Getting started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview"},"2230":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-0","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","content":"Create a CA, issue a client certificate and check its chain and key."},"2231":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-1","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#before-you-begin","content":"Before you begin"},"2232":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-2","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#recommended-path","content":"Recommended path"},"2233":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-3","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#expected-result","content":"Expected result"},"2234":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-4","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#continue-according-to-your-goal","content":"Continue according to your goal"},"2235":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-5","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","content":"This path is intended for those starting to administer PKI or needing a first X.509 client identity. It ends with three files: a root CA certificate, an end-entity certificate and the client's private key."},"2236":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-6","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#before-you-begin","content":"A Lamassu instance accessible from your browser. To prepare one, see Deployment."},"2237":